course: dictionary
lesson: 5200
title: What is Jainism?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jainism is a religion. It is an ancient religion from India, and it is still followed today. A religion is a set of beliefs about how people should live and what matters most in life.
explain: The most important idea in Jainism is ahimsa, which means never harming any living being. Because of this, many Jains are strict vegetarians, and some monks sweep the path in front of them so they do not step on insects.
explain: Jainism is studied in religious education lessons alongside Hinduism, Buddhism and Sikhism. The sentence «India has always been home to many peoples, languages and religions» gives a clue: it says that «Hinduism, Buddhism and Jainism began there», so Jainism began in India.
fact: Jainism is an ancient religion from India.
fact: «Hinduism, Buddhism and Jainism began there» tells us that Jainism began in India.
fact: Jains follow the teachings of Mahavira and earlier great teachers called Tirthankaras.
fact: Ahimsa means never harming any living being.
fact: Jains also value honesty, and they try to free the soul by living simply.
exercise: What is Jainism? | A sport played in schools | A type of bread from Australia | A language spoken in Scotland | *A very old religion from India
exercise: «India has always been home to many peoples, languages and religions.» According to the example sentence, where did Jainism begin? | Australia | London | *India | Scotland
exercise: Who do Jains follow the teachings of? | A football team | *Mahavira and earlier great teachers called Tirthankaras | The king of England | Scottish farmers
test: Why do some Jain monks sweep the path in front of them? | To clean it for the king | To find lost coins | To keep it dry | *So they do not step on insects
test: Which festival is important to Jains? | Christmas | Halloween | *Diwali | Bonfire Night
exam: The phrase «Jain temple» means what? | *A place of worship for Jains | A school for learning maths | A park with a lake | A shop that sells vegetables
